  ('104370160019708998', 'Such a Lovely Town...', 1979, 'Drama, Crime', 'Étienne Périer, Jean Charvein', 'André G. Brunelin, Étienne Périer', 'Jean Carmet, Victor Lanoux, Valérie Mairesse, Michel Robin, Jacques Richard, Gérard Jugnot, Francis Lemaire, Anne Bellec', null, 'Stephane (Victor Lanoux) is the mayor of a small village. He is also the manager of the tannery which provides the inhabitants with work. In a fit of anger, he kills his wife (Edith Scob). A judge (Jean Carmet) tries to prove his culpability, but it''s not an easy task, because there is a political and social pressure.', 'Stephane (Victor Lanoux) is the mayor of a small village. He is also the manager of the tannery which provides the inhabitants with work. In a fit of anger, he kills his wife (Edith Scob). A judge (Jean Carmet) tries to prove his culpability, but it''s not an easy task, because there is a political and social pressure.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/l4ZdidY7gtLC5AUCNVkchrCUwQG.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:42177'),
